WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:03.620
Priscilla: "Thou must returneth whence thou came."

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:08.040
"This land is peaceful, its inhabitants kind"

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:10.940
"But thou dost not belong."

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.860
Dark Souls 3 The Ashes of Ariandel drops on October 25th

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.500
And until then, I think you'll be impressed

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.520
With how much we can glean from a two minute trailer

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:28.800
The painted world of Ariamis was one of the most intricate late designed levels of Dark Souls 1

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:30.780
Accessed via a painting

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:33.560
Protected by the Painting Gardians, who

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:36.600
Have guarded the painting of Ariamis for so long

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.460
That their reason for doing so

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.560
Has long since past from memory

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.440
And Ariamis always was known to be a person

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:46.780
And he created this world with a purpose

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:51.980
Priscilla: "Didst thou not see why Ariamis created this world?"

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:55.160
The painted world is home to the unwanted

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:57.860
To the exiled and to the forlorn

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:02.060
"If you are like us another forlorn soul"

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.020
"With no place to call your own"

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:11.060
This piece of dialogue references two things

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:14.380
First, it references the Forlorn Set of Dark Souls 2

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:17.380
Which describes the forlorn invaders as

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:20.140
People without a world to call their own

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:23.760
Second, the other beings it could be referring to are

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:27.480
The Corvians, described by the Storyteller's Staff as

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:30.300
"Wretched beings with no place to go"

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:34.180
"Sharing tales of the Painted World to forlorn souls."

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:39.080
So already you're seeing a lot of characters from previous games mentioned here

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:42.180
And we talked about the Corvians in this video

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:46.640
We talked a lot about Velka and her crow symbology in this one

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:50.640
And I expect to see both related to this boss

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:55.320
This giant, violent womanly creature with a shawl of black feathers

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:58.480
In the concept art, it's even tied to a chair

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.400
Nailed to the ground

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:03.120
And in the video it's flagellating itself

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:06.780
While bent over this giant Lord vessel like bowl

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:10.640
Surrounding it are flammable wooden pillars

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:13.180
Which are reminiscent of those found in Lothric

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:16.880
And you probably learnt a new word, I know I did

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:19.480
Flagellation is a religious practice

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:22.880
Involving the mortification of one's own flesh

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:25.620
It's this act that seeks to put to death

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:27.600
One's sinful nature, and

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:31.460
It helps to separate oneself from your wordly desires

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:36.320
This reminds me of the mask of Velka's followers in Dark Souls 1, which

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:37.520
And I quote again:

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:41.080
"Symbolises their separation from worldly desires"

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:44.740
So flagellating yourself is very much related to Velka

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:48.800
And this boss has the crow feathers which is also related to her

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:53.480
Another slightly more tame example of mortification of flesh

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:56.500
Is the prostration pose, which is

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:59.960
This pose where you lower yourself to the ground submissively

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:02.020
And you kneel piously

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:04.780
The character in the trailer, he does this here

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:06.620
In the Cathedral of the Deep

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:10.260
Which leads me to believe that this NPC

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:13.300
Is likely the entrance point to the DLC

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:18.820
This man is offering us a beige and red sliver of canvas

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:23.560
Which is the exact same colour tone as the painting this girl sits at

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:27.180
And, as you know, touching the painting in Dark Souls 1

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:29.040
Was how we entered it, so

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:32.880
It looks like he's offering us a sliver of the painting also

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:36.100
And it makes a great deal of sense

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:39.460
For the painting to be related to the Cathedral of the Deep

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:44.140
For it was Aldrich who dreamt up the Miracle Lifehunt Scythe

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:47.720
Where he envisioned a pale girl in hiding

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:50.040
It should be pretty obvious who he envisioned

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:54.300
And it's his Deacons who surround the building below Yorshka

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:57.260
Where the original painting was once contained

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:02.460
And it's his Cathedral which makes the perfect early game entrance to the DLC

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:06.800
Not to mention this sword which is identical to the Candlesticks of the Deacons

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:11.480
A good question for this trailer is why does the man say:

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:16.640
"The ashes have come, at last."

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:20.260
I think it's possible he's talking about us, for

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:22.380
We are the unkindled ash, and

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:24.320
We represent the fact that

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:27.080
The fire has been linked so many times

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:30.840
That we are born from the ashes of the Undead who linked it

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:35.900
And, perhaps, our ash setting foot in the Painted World

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:37.300
Is a significant event

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:41.560
Or perhaps he's just talking about the actual Ashes of Ariandel

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:44.040
Which is something we don't know about yet

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:46.860
As the character arrives in the Painted World

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:49.520
Notice that the place looks to be

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:51.600
In better shape than in Dark Souls 1

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:54.980
Hell, the architecture even looks drastically different

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:58.540
The bridge is also unbroken, torches are lit

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:01.480
The main building isn't ruined at all and

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:04.780
There's even slivers of green at the end of the bridge

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:08.740
But so much is identical about this scene, though, and

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:13.160
It makes me wonder, how will they be putting a twist on this area?

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:15.800
How, from a story point of view at least,

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:18.640
Do you justify recycling the same zone?

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:23.080
My best guess is that this could be the Painted World of Ariandel

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:26.040
Not the world that Ariamis painted later

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:30.460
What if we are exploring the earlier painting of the world

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:32.580
Before it crumbled to ashes

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:36.500
And the painting of Ariamis is of the ruins it became?

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:41.640
I just really want to know what the architecture inside will look like

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:43.660
Look at this underground room for example

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:47.580
Doesn't it just look like the place you fought the Wheels Skeletons in Dark Souls 1?

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:51.620
I could be wrong about this but there even seems to be the wheel lever

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:53.900
That we turned to rotate the statue

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:56.340
All that time ago in Dark Souls 1, and

00:05:56.340 --> 00:06:00.420
This isn't a lever that's seen in any other part of Dark Souls 3, so...

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:04.020
But while we're speculating, let's move towards

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:07.060
The old bosses that were depicted in this trailer

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:10.580
At first, I thought that this part of the trailer with the old bosses

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:12.400
Was just cinematic filler

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:16.120
I thought that From Software didn't give Namco enough b-roll

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:18.200
To make their trailer, but

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:20.880
Really, all of these bosses are related

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:25.180
Literally, all are a part of the royal bloodline, in some way

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:28.080
Oceiros is husband to Queen Gwynevere

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:30.220
Who mothered Lothric and Lorian

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:33.500
And who is also sister to the Nameless King

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:36.240
And sister to Gwyndolin

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:38.460
Who Aldrich is consuming

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:40.660
And, apart from the bloodline stuff,

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:44.900
The Nameless King would certainly qualify as a forlorn exile

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:48.560
Oceiros appears to have bred a dragon crossbreed

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:50.500
Like Priscilla, and

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:53.140
Aldrich, of course, is the one who

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:56.440
Dreamt of the pale girl with Lifehunt Scythe

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:57.840
Who lies in hiding

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:01.440
Immediately following these clips is what looks like

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:04.120
A short cutscene, based on the camera angle

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:07.640
Where a character wearing Cornyx's set is

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:12.600
Exorcised of several yellow soul sprites in the Untended Graves

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:17.540
Curiously, his hand is burning like when it does when you link the fire

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:19.400
Maybe this is a new ending?

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:21.680
It doesn't look like he's casting a spell

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:24.240
But he is wearing Cornyx's set

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:27.880
So maybe they're implying that this is related to pyromancy?

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:30.800
I'm just rampant speculating, but it's interesting

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:33.320
In terms of gameplay addition, this image

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:36.060
Confirms the return of the PVP arena

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:40.520
As we see four players face off in the area we fought the Soul of Cinder

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:42.560
In terms of new spells,

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:45.500
You know I've gone on in the past about how spells

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:48.720
Need to be more than just simple projectiles that do

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:51.760
Varying amounts of damage at varying speeds

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:55.100
And at least two of the new spells in the DLC

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:56.380
Do look interesting

00:07:56.660 --> 00:08:00.120
This disc of light boomerang thing is great because

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:03.300
It requires you to position your character appropriately

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:05.420
To get a hit on the bounce back

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:09.340
And this frost sorcery could be interesting if

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:11.520
It actually slows our opponent and

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:14.780
Adds a element of crowd control into the magic system

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:16.480
Which I think it's all he needs

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:19.620
So colour me tentatively hyped for the new spells

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:24.820
But bear in mind, I've never actually been impressed with the spells they've added to a Soul game so...

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:28.400
The only new weapon seen is this axe

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:30.700
With the firestorm AoE effect

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:34.700
There this scimitar with a fairly standard spin weapon art

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:37.120
And of course the Candlestick Sword

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:39.880
That may or may not be buffing itself

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:41.920
With a type of colourless flame

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:45.020
Also, is there going to be a new torch

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:47.740
Added with this weapon art? Looks like it

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:50.700
New enemies include a wolf pack

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:52.280
There's the fly creatures

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:54.440
This stag-helmed warrior

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:57.260
A more deformed version of the Crow men

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:59.260
And you might have missed this but

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:03.700
In the blizzard are the silhouettes of dark-haired tree women

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:06.680
With small fires lit at the end of their branches

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:10.280
And to end the video, I'm going to pose to you

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:14.120
What I think are the biggest curiosities in the trailer

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:15.860
And in the DLC to come

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:18.860
First, the identity of this creature

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:21.480
I've seen speculation that it's Gwynevere

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:24.180
And the evidence for that is that it's clutching

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:26.380
A giant Lord Vessel like structure

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:29.360
And that it makes some sense for Gwynevere to have

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:32.260
Given up and been drawn into the Painted World

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:34.720
I've seen speculation that it's Velka

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:37.720
And I've mentioned before that that holds merit because

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:39.540
Of the crow symbology and

00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:42.260
Because of the theme of self-mortification

00:09:42.340 --> 00:09:44.580
That's brought up in the Black Set

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:47.740
What's more likely, though, than either of those two, I'd say

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:50.700
Is that it's some unnamed being

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:54.160
A simple Corvian perhaps, and it's even possible that

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.240
It's a man, not a woman,

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:59.160
Because the official Dark Souls Facebook page

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:01.160
Has labelled this as a man

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:04.180
However, I'm pretty sure that this page is run

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:06.660
By a simple marketing team, so

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:10.200
I'm not going to put too much faith in their captions

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:15.260
Second, I want to know who the man is who brings us to this world

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:16.540
Is it Ariamis?

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:20.800
Is Ariandel the female depicted upon the painter's ladder?

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:24.640
Is it her world, or is it still Ariamis's?

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:27.080
And this piece of narration is interesting:

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:30.180
"Then show my Lady flame"

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:33.200
Why does she need to be shown flame?

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:38.020
Does she want to see our flame so she can paint a new vision perhaps?

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:40.640
And what are the Ashes of Ariandel?

00:10:40.920 --> 00:10:44.200
In Souls, ashes are remains, so

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:47.580
I'm not too sure that Ariandel's fate is a happy one

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:49.000
Is this wolf Sif?

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:52.400
It certainly seems larger than the other wolves

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:54.520
Look at the trees for comparison

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:58.120
But Sif has no real connections to this place

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:00.340
And most importantly

00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:03.240
Why does the boss attack us with Estus soup?

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:04.500
Time will tell

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:08.620
And by the way remember, I recently did a lot of postulating on

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:12.620
How I thought the two most likely themes for the DLC would be

00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:15.280
The Angels of Lothric of the Hollows of Londor

00:11:15.280 --> 00:11:17.020
And you can see these videos here

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:19.980
But I couldn't be happier that they seem to be throwing us

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:22.760
A sort of curve ball, as usual, and

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:26.240
They're hitting us with something we didn't quite expect to see

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:29.580
And it's not too late to talk about the Angels of the Hollows

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:32.780
This DLC could still answer some of those questions

00:11:32.780 --> 00:11:35.460
Maybe some answers about Gwynevere's royal family

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:37.260
Exist in the Painted World, or

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:40.200
Maybe we'll learn about the significance of Velka

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:42.840
Through the crow symbology or something like that

00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:45.480
So, on October 25th,

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:47.440
Two months from now, I hope you make

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:49.440
This channel the place to be, but

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:52.300
Until then, let's get into some "Prepare to Cry"

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:53.760
Thanks for watching guys

